          %p
            Since
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma \,\coloneqq\,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/PU%28%E2%84%8B%29"} PU(ℋ)
            is not a (finite-dimensional)
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nearby+homomorphisms+from+compact+Lie+groups+are+conjugate"} nearby homomorphisms from compact Lie groups are conjugate
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domain"} domain
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+group"} discrete
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+group"} finite group
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/PU%28%E2%84%8B%29"} PU(ℋ)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-space"} -space
            of homomorphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Hom
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi PU
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℋ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom\big(G,\, PU(\mathcal{H})\big)
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+union"} disjoint union
            (
            %a{:href => "nearby+homomorphisms+from+compact+Lie+groups+are+conjugate#eq:DisjointUnionOfOrbits"}> as here
            ) of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbits"} orbits
            of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjugation+action"} conjugation action
          %p
            This is established in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#UribeLueck13"} Uribe &amp; Lück 2013, Sec. 15
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/pdf/1304.4862.pdf#page=38"} p. 38
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/U%28%E2%84%8B%29"} U(ℋ)
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+equivariant+PU%28H%29-bundle"}
                  universal equivariant
                  = succeed "-bundle" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi PU
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi ℋ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PU(\mathcal{H})
          %h2#literature Literature
          %blockquote
            %p
              Cf. also the
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "UH#References"}
                  references at
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi.mathscript ℋ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(\mathscr{H})
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi.mathscript ℋ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(\mathscr{H})
              were not a topological group in the strong operator topology.
          %p General discussion:
          %ul
            %li#Simms68
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+John+Simms"}> David John Simms
                , pp. 5 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Lie Groups and Quantum Mechanics
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 52
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BFb0069914"} doi:10.1007/BFb0069914
            %li#Simms70
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+John+Simms"}> David John Simms
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Topological aspects of the projective unitary group
                %strong 68
                1 (1970) 57-60 (
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/S0305004100001043"}> doi:10.1017/S0305004100001043
                )
            %li#UribeLueck13
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bernardo+Uribe"}> Bernardo Uribe
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wolfgang+L%C3%BCck"} Wolfgang Lück
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Equivariant principal bundles and their classifying spaces
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1304.4862"} arXiv:1304.4862
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.2140/agt.2014.14.1925"} doi:10.2140/agt.2014.14.1925
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jesus+Espinoza"}> Jesus Espinoza
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bernardo+Uribe"} Bernardo Uribe
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Topological properties of spaces of projective unitary representations
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1511.06785"} arXiv:1511.06785
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.scielo.org.co/scielo.php?script=sci_arttext&pid=S0370-39082016000200013"} scielo:S0370-39082016000200013
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.18257/raccefyn.317"} doi:10.18257/raccefyn.317
          %p Concerning well-pointedness:
          %ul
            %li#HebestreitSagave19
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fabian+Hebestreit"}> Fabian Hebestreit
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Steffen+Sagave"} Steffen Sagave
              = succeed "," do
                %em Homotopical and operator algebraic twisted K-theory
              %strong 378
              (2020) 1021-1059 (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1904.01872"}> arXiv:1904.01872
              ,
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s00208-020-02066-6"} doi:10.1007/s00208-020-02066-6
          %p
            The
            = succeed "-graded" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
